SELF-CHECK -- an alarm that has fired for real
A completing gate verifies EVERY criterion twice and then red-teams
them, so it cannot cost less than one sweep. When this bench was first
written it did, because the fixture was reused across samples and four
of five samples measured the dormant hook. That bug is now an assertion:
  CONSISTENT   completing gate 5646 ms >= one sweep 1546 ms

NOT MEASURED HERE: your verify commands. In real use they dominate
everything above -- the engine's own overhead is a rounding error next
to a test suite, and that is the intended trade.
